{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787426247626,"sessionID":"ses_fd518000affe6KchMdNdr1keVe","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_kvg0db4j","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-c30U4X/checkout/benchmark"},"output":"<path>/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-c30U4X/checkout/benchmark</path>\n<type>directory</type>\n<entries>\nenvironment/\nruns/\nschemas/\nSTUDY.md\ntasks/\n\n(5 entries)\n</entries>","metadata":{"preview":"environment/\nruns/\nschemas/\nSTUDY.md\ntasks/","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"directory","path":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-c30U4X/checkout/benchmark","entries":["environment/","runs/","schemas/","STUDY.md","tasks/"],"offset":1,"totalEntries":5,"truncated":false}},"title":"benchmark","time":{"start":1787426247621,"end":1787426247625}},"id":"prt_02ae813c30013rj6iUpdaqvHkv","sessionID":"ses_fd518000affe6KchMdNdr1keVe","messageID":"msg_02ae8091b002trs5W3rteCaQvc"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787426247629,"sessionID":"ses_fd518000affe6KchMdNdr1keVe","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_dq6aowxw","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-c30U4X/checkout/README.md"},"output":"<path>/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-c30U4X/checkout/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Coding Assistant Study Plan\n2: \n3: An interactive six-week playbook for comparing:\n4: \n5: - Codex, Claude Code, and OpenCode as coding assistants\n6: - Pi as a neutral model harness\n7: - OpenAI and Anthropic frontier models\n8: - DeepSeek and Kimi through Ollama Cloud, plus a small local Qwen control\n9: - Skills, plugins, MCP servers, hooks, permissions, and multi-agent workflows\n10: \n11: The plan separates assistant effects from model effects, defines a 94-run core\n12: study, and ends with a distributed project led by a frontier model and completed\n13: by smaller workers.\n14: \n15: ## Local use\n16: \n17: ```bash\n18: npm install\n19: npm run dev\n20: ```\n21: \n22: Open the local URL shown in the terminal. Progress checkboxes are stored only in\n23: the browser on that device. Use the **Print / save PDF** action for a static copy.\n24: \n25: ## Verification\n26: \n27: ```bash\n28: npm run verify\n29: ```\n30: \n31: ## Benchmark setup\n32: \n33: The reproducible study contract is in `benchmark/STUDY.md`. The first frozen\n34: task is a read-only repository analysis with a 100-point rubric.\n35: \n36: ```bash\n37: npm run benchmark:env\n38: npm run benchmark:validate\n39: npm run benchmark:run -- --assistant opencode\n40: ```\n41: \n42: The last command is a safe preview. Add `--execute` to create a unique evidence\n43: folder in `benchmark/runs/`. Generated runs are ignored by Git and never\n44: overwritten.\n45: \n46: Model and product details in the plan were researched on August 22, 2026. Record\n47: the exact assistant version and model ID again before every study block.\n\n(End of file - total 47 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Coding Assistant Study Plan\n\nAn interactive six-week playbook for comparing:\n\n- Codex, Claude Code, and OpenCode as coding assistants\n- Pi as a neutral model harness\n- OpenAI and Anthropic frontier models\n- DeepSeek and Kimi through Ollama Cloud, plus a small local Qwen control\n- Skills, plugins, MCP servers, hooks, permissions, and multi-agent workflows\n\nThe plan separates assistant effects from model effects, defines a 94-run core\nstudy, and ends with a distributed project led by a frontier model and completed\nby smaller workers.\n\n## Local use\n\n```bash\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-c30U4X/checkout/README.md","text":"# Coding Assistant Study Plan\n\nAn interactive six-week playbook for comparing:\n\n- Codex, Claude Code, and OpenCode as coding assistants\n- Pi as a neutral model harness\n- OpenAI and Anthropic frontier models\n- DeepSeek and Kimi through Ollama Cloud, plus a small local Qwen control\n- Skills, plugins, MCP servers, hooks, permissions, and multi-agent workflows\n\nThe plan separates assistant effects from model effects, defines a 94-run core\nstudy, and ends with a distributed project led by a frontier model and completed\nby smaller workers.\n\n## Local use\n\n```bash\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nOpen the local URL shown in the terminal. Progress checkboxes are stored only in\nthe browser on that device. Use the **Print / save PDF** action for a static copy.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\nnpm run verify\n```\n\n## Benchmark setup\n\nThe reproducible study contract is in `benchmark/STUDY.md`. The first frozen\ntask is a read-only repository analysis with a 100-point rubric.\n\n```bash\nnpm run benchmark:env\nnpm run benchmark:validate\nnpm run benchmark:run -- --assistant opencode\n```\n\nThe last command is a safe preview. Add `--execute` to create a unique evidence\nfolder in `benchmark/runs/`. Generated runs are ignored by Git and never\noverwritten.\n\nModel and product details in the plan were researched on August 22, 2026. Record\nthe exact assistant version and model ID again before every study block.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":47,"totalLines":47,"truncated":false}},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1787426247611,"end":1787426247628}},"id":"prt_02ae813b2001v3HIRK6XQM1Bai","sessionID":"ses_fd518000affe6KchMdNdr1keVe","messageID":"msg_02ae8091b002trs5W3rteCaQvc"}}
