{"type":"text","timestamp":1787426266065,"sessionID":"ses_fd518000affe6KchMdNdr1keVe","part":{"id":"prt_02ae8471f001bIp46EVHfx0Toz","messageID":"msg_02ae842dc002pIMVWNiJMbnyVx","sessionID":"ses_fd518000affe6KchMdNdr1keVe","type":"text","text":"# Repository analysis report\n\n## Architecture\n\nThis is a **read-only analysis task** (benchmark task `T1-repo-map`). I inspected the listed files; all claims below are grounded in those.\n\n**Purpose:** An interactive six-week study plan comparing coding assistants (Codex, Claude Code, OpenCode) and models, with a reproducible benchmark harness for grading assistant runs. It is also the very repository the benchmark runs against.\n\n**Tech:** Next.js 16 (React 19, RSC) served via **Vinext** + Vite on **Cloudflare Workers** (Wrangler/Miniflare), Drizzle ORM (D1), Tailwind 4, TypeScript 5.9. Node >=22. `package.json:2-21`.\n\n**Key dirs:**\n- `app/` — the study site. `app/page.tsx` is the entire single-page client component; `app/layout.tsx` wraps it (metadata + fonts); `app/chatgpt-auth.ts` is optional ChatGPT auth helpers (currently unused in `page.tsx`).\n- `worker/index.ts` — Cloudflare Worker entry; routes image optimization and delegates to the Vinext app-router handler (`worker/index.ts:32`).\n- `scripts/` — benchmark runner, environment writer, and validator. `benchmark-run.mjs` is the core harness.\n- `benchmark/` — the frozen research contract: `STUDY.md`, versioned tasks (`benchmark/tasks/T1-repo-map/`), schemas, and generated `runs/`.\n- `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs` — smoke test that server-renders the page.\n- `db/` — Drizzle (schema currently empty). `build/`, `drizzle/`, `examples/` support tooling.\n\n## Main request flow\n\nFor a study-site request: the Cloudflare Worker `fetch` (`worker/index.ts:29`) delegates to `vinext/server/app-router-entry`, which routes to Next app-router code. `app/layout.tsx` supplies the shell; `app/page.tsx` (a `\"use client\"` component) renders all sections from in-memory arrays (e.g., `stages` at `page.tsx:257`, `taskRows` at `page.tsx:158`). The response is server-rendered HTML.\n\nFor a benchmark run: `npm run benchmark:run` (read `scripts/benchmark-run.mjs`) reads the task's `prompt.md`, builds a per-assistant command adapter (`benchmark-run.mjs:123-212`), snapshots the workspace, executes the assistant in an isolated worktree, diffs the snapshot, and writes `manifest.json`, `prompt.md`, `stdout.log`, `stderr.log`, `changes.json`, `result.json` into a unique `benchmark/runs/<run-id>/` (`benchmark-run.mjs:277-363`). Read-only mode auto-fails if any path changed (`benchmark-run.mjs:331-333`).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm run typecheck` — `tsc --noEmit`; proves TypeScript types compile.\n- `npm run lint` — ESLint over the repo; proves code style/static rules.\n- `npm test` — builds then runs `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs`; proves the built app server-renders key strings with a 200 HTML response.\n- `npm run verify` — runs all of the above plus `benchmark:validate`; the full gate.\n- `npm run benchmark:env` / `benchmark:env:write` — checks / records the environment.\n- `npm run benchmark:validate` — validates task/schema/run contracts.\n- `npm run benchmark:run` — executes/records a run (needs `--execute`); preview mode is safe.\n\n## Risks and unknowns\n\n1. **Evidence:** `db/schema.ts` is empty but `getDb()` (`db/index.ts:5`) throws if the D1 binding is absent, and `chatgpt-auth.ts` is written but unreferenced — dead/placeholder scaffolding whose behavior isn't exercised by `tests/`.\n2. **Evidence:** `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs` depends on a successful build and exact HTML strings; it will break if any asserted copy changes and does not test the `\"use client\"` interactivity (checkboxes/localStorage) or `chatgpt-auth`.\n3. **Inference:** `benchmark-run.mjs` assumes external CLIs (`codex`, `claude`, `opencode`, `pi`, `ollama`) exist in PATH; failure handling and timeout semantics (`SIGTERM` kill) rely on child-process close events that could flake in CI. The task is frozen (read-only); prompt/model identity is deliberately stripped from prompts (`task.json`).\n\n## Small change plan — add visible \"pilot completed\" status\n\n1. **Read** `app/page.tsx` to find where pilot status should surface (e.g., near `benchmarkLanes` render at `page.tsx:639` or the `first-run` block at `page.tsx:1057`); decide the trigger source.\n2. **Add a boolean/computed value** derived from the existing `completed` state (`page.tsx:391-417`) or a new constant, plus a styled badge in JSX with accessible text (matching existing class conventions).\n3. **Verify** via `npm run build` and `npm test`; add/update a marker string in `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs` if asserting the new text server-renders.\n4. **Run** `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint` to confirm no type/style regressions.\n5. **Confirm** no change to frozen `benchmark/` files; verify the site renders the badge locally with `npm run dev` (browser check), and keep the diff to the single `app/` files.","time":{"start":1787426260767,"end":1787426266060}}}
